            <div xml:id="d931">

                <pb facs="0840" n="724" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg724"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2871.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Ciudad
                            Juárez to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Ciudad Juárez</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">via
                                El Paso, Tex.</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1912-02-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 23, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Discontent and disorganization growing. A general exodus to the United States
                    continues and attack on Juárez expected. Railroad traffic not attempted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwards.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
